    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today hinges on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who anchors our offense with a 67.10 efficiency score. Facing Legumina, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.32 xERA matchup and an 8% boost from batting second, making him our premier start. **Drake Baldwin** follows as the next most viable option at 59.15; while he draws a tougher look against Hart, his lead-off spot provides significant runway to contribute to our R and RBI totals. We are playing a cautious game with **Brayan Rocchio** and **Dominic Smith** today; **Brayan Rocchio** sits at a marginal 44.53, held back by a difficult matchup against Bradley, while **Dominic Smith** is teetering on the edge of our bench floor at 40.68 due to a disadvantageous lefty-on-lefty platoon split against Hart.\n\nOur bench strategy remains dictated by extreme caution regarding game caps. We are currently resting our high-ceiling core\u2014including **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014as their teams are off today, providing us a necessary window to preserve our innings and games-played allocations. **Jackson Merrill** was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but his sub-zero adjusted score, triggered by a brutal matchup against Sale and a projected bottom-of-the-order assignment, made him an easy exclusion. While we have depth in reserve like **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Heliot Ramos**, we are prioritizing efficiency over volume today. We must remain vigilant regarding **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith**, as any late-breaking lineup changes regarding their order placement could quickly push them below our 40.00 floor, forcing us to pivot to bench assets like **Nasim Nunez** or **Sam Antonacci** if we need to chase stolen bases in a pinch.",
